jobs.description:
As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.

Are you looking for an active job with lots of variety? At FedEx in Duiven, you will contribute to a global logistics process. Your efforts ensure that packages reach their destination on time. In return, you will receive an attractive salary of €15,16 per hour, with shift allowances up to €21,22. Both 32-hour and 40-hour workweeks are possible.

What are you going to do?
In this dynamic role, you ensure that everything runs smoothly in the sorting process. Your tasks include:

- Sorting and processing incoming parcels;
- Transporting packages using a forklift;
- Efficiently loading parcels into trucks;
- Collaborating with colleagues to meet deadlines.
- You will work in the following shifts:

14:30 – 23:00

17:30 – 01:00

23:00 – 07:00

What do we offer?
- Gross hourly wage of €15.16, with allowances up to €21,22 per hour;
- Prospect of a permanent contract with FedEx;
- 8% holiday allowance and 25 vacation days;
- Travel allowance of €0.25 per kilometer;
- Pension accrual via Adecco from the age of 18;
- Access to the Adecco Academy for training and courses;
- A pleasant, safe working environment with supportive colleagues.

Where will you work?
FedEx is one of the largest logistics service providers in the world and ships millions of parcels daily from Duiven to more than 200 countries. Working safely, collaborating, and continuous growth are central values. Your contribution is seen and appreciated.

What do we ask?
- You speak Dutch and/or English;
- You are able to apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG) (costs will be reimbursed);
- You have your own transportation to Duiven;
- You have experience operating a forklift or are willing to learn;
- You are flexible and available for different shifts.

Are you interested?
Ready to get started? Click the apply button before September 26 , 2026 and take the next step in your career!

Questions? Call or WhatsApp Sanne at 06 42806892.

Are you looking for a warehouse job in an international team with clear working hours and opportunities to grow? Start as a Warehouse Employee at GXO Logistics in Tilburg. You earn €14.99 gross per hour and receive travel allowance and pension.

You work with clothing and accessories. Depending on your department, you collect, pack, check or move products.

Your tasks can include:

- Picking orders with a scanner;
- Packing and checking products;
- Processing returned items;
- Receiving and storing products;
- Preparing orders for shipment;
- Keeping your workplace clean and safe.

You will receive training for the tasks in your department. There are also opportunities to learn different warehouse processes.

You work either a fixed morning shift or in two shifts:

- Morning shift: 06:00 to 14:45;
- Afternoon shift: 15:15 to 00:00.

You like active work and enjoy working together with others.

We ask:

- You speak English at B1 level or higher;
- You are physically fit and can stand and walk for longer periods;
- You are available for a fixed morning shift or two-shift schedule;
- You have your own accommodation and transport;
- You can apply for a Certificate of Good Conduct (VOG);
- You are available full-time.

Experience in a warehouse is useful, but not listed as a requirement for this job.
